 arbace: RFC 8446, Section 4.2.11"] [361 4 "// Server selected a cipher suite incompatible with the PSK."] [373 3 "// Any extensions which have changed in hello, but are mirrored in the"] [374 3 "// outer hello and compressed, need to be copied to the outer hello, so"] [375 3 "// they can be properly decompressed by the server. For now, the only"] [376 3 "// extension which may have changed is keyShares."] [394 2 "// serverHelloMsg is not included in the transcript"] [541 3 "// RFC 8446 specifies that no_application_protocol is sent by servers, but"] [542 3 "// does not specify how clients handle the selection of an incompatible protocol."] [543 3 "// RFC 9001 Section 8.1 specifies that QUIC clients send no_application_protocol"] [544 3 "// in this case. Always sending no_application_protocol seems reasonable."] [552 4 "// RFC 9001 Section 8.2."] [596 2 "// Either a PSK or a certificate is always used, but not both."] [597 2 "// See RFC 8446, Section 4.1.1."] [599 3 "// Make sure the connection is still being verified whether or not this"] [600 3 "// is a resumption. Resumptions currently don't reverify certificates so"] [601 3 "// they don't call verifyServerCertificate. See Issue 31641."] [604 37 "// arbace"] [618 52 "// arbace: as before, a decode error"] [635 85 "// arbace: context"] [647 2 "// certificateVerifyMsg is included in the transcript, but not until"] [648 2 "// after we verify the handshake signature, since the state before"] [649 2 "// this message was sent is used."] [661 2 "// See RFC 8446, Section 4.4.3."] [662 2 "// We don't use hs.hello.supportedSignatureAlgorithms because it might"] [663 2 "// include PKCS#1 v1.5 and SHA-1 if the ClientHello also supported TLS 1.2."] [694 2 "// finishedMsg is included in the transcript, but not until after we"] [695 2 "// check the client version, since the state before this message was"] [696 2 "// sent is used during verification."] [718 2 "// Derive secrets that take context through the server Finished."] [7